  "name": "The Exponentiation Property",
  "problem": "The multiplicative property states that given $a \\equiv b \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\,n)$ and $c \\equiv d \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\,n),$ we obtain $ac \\equiv bd \\: (\\textrm{mod}\\,n).$ By taking the same congruence twice, we obtain \n\n$$\na^2 \\equiv b^2  \\qquad (\\textrm{mod}\\,n).\n$$\n\nIn general, \n\n$$\na^k \\equiv b^k  \\qquad (\\textrm{mod}\\,n)\n$$\n\nfor any *positive* integer $k.$",
